"""opos-selftest: read-only acceptance checks of a running OPOS OS on the Surface Duo.

One line per check, "STATUS id evidence", STATUS being PASS, FAIL, WARN or SKIP; the exit status is 1 when any
line is FAIL. It needs no root and runs as the droidian user over ssh. It reads /proc, /sys, /etc, /var and /opt,
asks systemctl, journalctl, timedatectl, ip, nmcli and wlr-randr for status only (run() refuses any other
command or verb) and sends HTTP GETs to the OPOS server on loopback. It writes nothing and changes nothing.

PASS is evidence that a thing works from this side (a process, a sysfs value, an HTTP answer); it is not a look at
the glass. The checks that need eyes and hands are in docs/duo-acceptance.md.

Test seams (arguments, never environment): --root, --bin, --url, --now.
"""
